  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday)\nIssued at 147 AM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nEnsemble signal remains consistent in showing an unseasonably strong \nupper ridge remaining centered near/across our area into next week, \ndespite at least one stronger upper trough continuing to impinge \nfrom the west. This will keep the streak of upper-90s to mid-100s \nafternoon highs and >105 deg F heat indices rolling on into next \nweek. While nil chance for precipitation is currently advertised in \nour forecast, can't rule out the low chance for diurnal \nshowers/storms on Monday across eastern Oklahoma.\n\nThe big question is when exactly the pattern breaks, even for just a \nfew days. Right now, there is *some/modest* signal in ensemble and \ndeterministic guidance that potential for precipitation and \nperhaps moderated temperatures arrives by next weekend \n(12th-14th). Something we will be watching with keen interest over\nthe coming days.\n\nUngar",
